// Actor shadows on lightmapped surfaces (the A6 planar shadow's replacement; under shadows=rt the planar pass is never
// drawn). The lightmaps already hold the static light and its world shadows, so only models with the original SHADOW
// flag (TLAS mask 4) are traced, toward the lights of render_policy::actor_shadow_lights (baked WMB and native point/spot
// lights whose range holds a caster, and the sun), toward a point jittered within clamp(0.005 range, 0.5, 2) units (lamp
// bulbs are small: the 2-12 unit soft-shadow sphere blurred a body's shadow away a few metres from it). Weight: luma x N.L
// x falloff (baked: linear 1 - d/range; native: its D3D attenuation and cone; sun: 1), at most 1. A blocked baked light
// counts only where the level geometry lets it reach the receiver (else the lightmap holds none of it); the sun counts only
// there at all, so indoor levels get no sun shadow.
// Darkness = SHADOW_ALPHA x min(occluded weight / strongest weight, 1): blocking the receiver's dominant light darkens it
// like the original planar shadow, a weaker light gives a proportionally lighter shadow. Where even the strongest light
// is faint (weight below 0.02) or no light reaches at all, the shadow blends into one cast toward the planar shadow's own
// light direction (g.planar, at SHADOW_ALPHA, regardless of the level geometry like the planar shadow), so every caster
// keeps a shadow close to the original's. Per pixel and frame: the dominant light, one other light picked in proportion
// to its weight (it stands for all the others), and the sun.
